Give a project the repositories its sandbox sessions clone.

Project settings get a Repositories field when the project's host is the
sandbox or no default: the composer's GitHub repository and branch pickers
(made modal so their lists scroll inside the dialog), plus a field to paste any
other URL, which Save keeps even when it wasn't added. They're stored in the
project's config as sandbox_repos; the server keeps a project's config whole,
so no server change is needed. A concrete host drops them, and for the sandbox
the working directory field is hidden, as the composer does.
A new session in the project picks them in place of the last repositories
launched with, once the project's config has loaded, unless the user already
changed the selection (tracked in the parked draft too). A project without
repositories keeps the last ones.
Base: omnigent v0.18.0 (a8676d23e88d).
